    "committedAt": "2026-11-06T15:45:29Z",
    "message": "fix(tickets): read frontmatter with PyYAML instead of a hand-rolled parser (#3169)\n\nThe hand-rolled reader kept `# comment` text in bare values, so\n`status: done # merged` read as an unknown status and blocked its ticket,\nand it split inline lists on commas inside quotes.\n\n- tickets.py declares pyyaml in its PEP 723 header; every caller already\n  runs it through `uv run`.\n- FrontmatterLoader types only whole numbers, true, false and null; every\n  other scalar stays text, so `after: [1.10]` is entry 10 in epic 1 and a\n  date is the text it was written as. An absent value reads as \"\".\n- Invalid YAML is refused with the file and line.\n- Edits stay one-line replaces, checked: the frontmatter must read as\n  before with only the edited keys changed, or the edit is refused\n  unwritten with \"edit the frontmatter by hand\".\n- Reads accept block lists, so the inline-only rule and lenient mode go.\n- quoted() escapes every non-printable character.\n\nFixes #3136"
  },
